Being a bit less altruistic in my approach to Nethack than some,
I have been playing some of the "hack and slash" characters. 
Specifically, I just played Conehead the Barbarian and happened
to run into a level which had both a barracks and an altar.  Since
I was already at level 14 with Excal and some half decent armour,
I decided to go for it.  When I was done, I had summoned several
demons and two demon lords (jubilex and yeenoghu - sp?) who just
wandered around gurgling, grunting or being stoic.  Is there any
benefit to summoning these nasty dudes?  None of them attacked me
nor were any of them tame, they were all peaceful and would follow
me downstairs if I was patient enough.  I found the whole experience
somewhat depressing; after all, I had just sacrificed about a dozen
soldiers (some captains and sargeants too) and got nothing for it
but a few scratches and some rather dull dungeon mates.  Is there
any point to even bothering with this?  If so, what is it?  
 
Oh, and as my obligatory brag, I ascended with 163 hit points,
-21 AC (6 of which were due to a now wealthy priestess of Nuada),
level 15, just about every intrinsic going (I found a tinning kit
and managed to tin a few puddin's along the way) A of Reflection,
a blessed luckstone (found it in hell of all places), and one or
two rings (conflict was nice in the end game, but those rust monster
are dull to watch when they fight one another).  I ended up with a 
measly 1004525 points (no gold, no gems) after 47692 turns.  I could
have kept the number of turns down much lower, but I didn't trust
the means of locating the level of the wiz and teleported way past
him and had to climb up ten extra levels.  Who would have believed
that the castle was on level 29 and the wizard on 31?  I sure didn't
 
Anyway, looking forward to your comments on the use and care of
demons
 
